onal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $b=6,$ $c=5,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{6}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81211/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b15719b6-0ce4-5fb8-80be-abcaf9344a10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81211"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-41034/selection/db7b536abbfbcf7bf94ee6f7b1bfcfcde80a4b0681c0d4a814e23a1769d0dc6f" :answer/id #uuid "7c15b356-678e-518e-9a6a-5deb3b77100e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41034/selection/e23f9ea338f175b3f5a7621b94518bec0d179d6cb526e41f