\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 3+0\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+7\\cdot 0}{{3}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{0}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=-\\sqrt{3},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{-\\sqrt{3}}{1}=-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-41034/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b15719b6-0ce4-5fb8-80be-abcaf9344a10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-41034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40742/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "d20709ae-a847-51de-8e0a-8b009b573ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" 